# Per Vercel's Rust runtime docs: ignore the cargo target/ directory
# except for release binaries (Vercel needs them to package the
# function bundle). The local cache is huge (gigabytes) and shouldn't
# upload as part of the deploy.
target/**
!target/release
!target/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/release/**
!target/aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu/release/**

# engine/ workspace's own target dir — same reasoning. We only need
# the engine source tree on Vercel (so the root Cargo.toml's path
# deps resolve), not its compiled artefacts.
engine/target/**
